Done. Both `npm run typecheck` and `npm test` (15 tests) pass.

## What I changed

**`src/types.ts`** — Added `"market"` to the `BuildingKind` union.

**`src/buildings/registry.ts`** — Registered the market in the single source of truth:
```ts
market: { cost: { wood: 20, stone: 15 }, requires: "storehouse" },
```
Also added `market: "production"` to the `BUILDING_CATEGORY` map (TS requires every `BuildingKind` to have a category; the LSP flagged this, and a market produces stone so "production" fits). Updated the prerequisite-chain comment to note the new branch. Because `availability.ts` reads `requires` from this table, the storehouse prerequisite is enforced automatically — no build() change needed.

**`src/sim/trade.ts`** (new) — Implements `sellResource`:
- Throws if no market is built.
- Sells `min(available, amount)`, never taking the resource below 0.
- Converts at 2:1, `Math.floor`, crediting the resulting stone.
- Returns a new settlement (input untouched).

**`src/sim/index.ts`** — Added `export { sellResource } from "./trade";` (re-exported transitively via `src/index.ts`'s `export * from "./sim"`).

## One bug I caught and fixed

My first draft only debited the sold resource and forgot to credit the earned stone — my verification test caught it (stone stayed at 0). Fixed by chaining two `credit()` calls from `resources/costs.ts`, which the existing docs had already flagged as the intended trade.ts helper.

Files under the disposable run root only; no source fixtures or sibling checkouts touched.


